The plate looks like a side plate or small dinner plate, roughly 20-22 cm across. On it is a small pile of what looks like cauliflower or mashed potato, topped with fresh pico de gallo (tomato and onion) and a green salsa.

I'd estimate about 150 g of food in total: roughly 80 g of the white base, 50 g of pico, and 20 g of salsa. The white base is probably around 60 kcal per 100 g, which gives about 50-80 kcal. The tomato and salsa add about 25 kcal. Any oil would add more, so I'll allow for that and settle on roughly 120 kcal.

